.TH BIGNUMS 7 "2026-09-22" "BigNums" "Miscellaneous Information Manual"
.nr HY 0
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
bignums \- fixed-capacity big integer and binary floating-point library
.SH DESCRIPTION
BigNums is a C99 library for unsigned integers and signed binary floats.
It uses little-endian arrays of 256 32-bit limbs and FFT integer multiplication.
Float operations use exact integer intermediates, scaled division, and
integer square roots.
Numbers have fixed storage: at most 8192 integer or mantissa bits.
Unsigned integers range from 0 through 2^8192 \- 1.
The BigFloat exponent remains a signed 32-bit count of binary positions.
.PP
The larger storage changes the layout of BigInt and BigFloat.
Rebuild the library and its applications together when upgrading from the
128-limb version; old compiled objects are not binary-compatible.
The SONAME remains libbignums.so.0 and does not distinguish these layouts.
.SH GETTING STARTED
On Linux with an ELF toolchain and GNU Make, run ./build.sh from the repository
root to build and install the shared library, headers, and manuals.
The default prefix is $HOME/.local; override it with PREFIX=/usr/local when
you have write access to that prefix.  The script calls man_setup.sh to install
manuals under PREFIX/share/man/man3 and man7.
Prefix-based installation does not invoke sudo.
.PP
For standard system-wide linking, run ./build.sh \-\-system.
It builds first, then uses sudo unless already root to install into /usr/local.
It registers /usr/local/lib in /etc/ld.so.conf.d/bignums.conf and runs ldconfig.
On a standard native Linux toolchain, an application can then be compiled with:
.PP
.EX
cc app.c \-lbignums \-o app
.EE
.PP
System mode requires Linux/glibc and ldconfig, and accepts no path overrides.
DESTDIR supports package staging; it is not included in runtime paths.
.PP
Include bignums.h and link an application against the installed library:
.PP
.EX
cc app.c \e
    \-I"$HOME/.local/include" \e
    \-L"$HOME/.local/lib" \e
    \-Wl,\-rpath,"$HOME/.local/lib" \e
    \-lbignums \-o app
.EE
.PP
The library filename is libbignums.so.0.1.0, with SONAME libbignums.so.0 and
relative symlinks for the SONAME and linker name libbignums.so.
The rpath controls runtime lookup; the linker search option alone does not.
The shared library records its dependency on the math library.
Applications that call math functions directly should also link with \-lm.
.PP
Alternatively, compile with both library sources from the bigNums directory:
.PP
.EX
cc \-std=c99 \-O2 program.c bigNumLibThingy.c \e
    smartFFTThingy.c \-lm \-o program
.EE
.PP
The math library must be linked after the source/object files that use it.
There is no required FFT-header inclusion order for applications using only
the number API.
.PP
From the repository root, build and run the examples and tests with:
.PP
.EX
make \-C bigNums shared
make \-C bigNums test demo
\&./build/demo
.EE
.PP
The default Make target builds only the shared library under build/lib.
Supply MAIN to also build a custom driver.  The test and demo targets build
executables under build that load the shared library using a relative rpath;
the test target also runs the numerical suite.
The numerical test executable returns nonzero if a check fails.
